From 9f67fdc2c8e708f73c6ebca949a8bfc7dc65e8b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (audit)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:16:41 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 07/14] frontend: harden the API client and session handling

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011d4mgSxngjRmAXosGe4ry4

- Drop the hidden localStorage 'tuitiontrack_api_url' override (anything able to
  write localStorage could redirect every request and password to another host).
- Content-Type only on requests with a body (no CORS preflight on every GET).
- Network failures become a readable offline message; errors carry status,
  code and fieldErrors from the API's {message, code, errors} shape.
- A failed page while collecting a paginated list is an error, not a silently
  short list.
- Refresh: only a 400/401 refusal signs the user out; an offline refresh or a
  server hiccup keeps the session. The single-flight promise resets
  immediately instead of on a timer.
- Server clock offset comes from /meta/ and is measured once for all exam cards
  (was a HEAD /auth/me/ per card).
- AuthProvider no longer signs the user out when /auth/me/ fails offline;
  useAuth moved to context/auth.js.
- Remove dead legacy endpoints (batches, 1-on-1 cycles, unused details); add
  splitHomework.
